A Red-Black Tree is a self-balancing binary search tree where each node is colored either red or black. 
These trees maintain balance through specific coloring rules, ensuring O(log n) performance for search, insert, 
and delete operations.

Key Properties
Color Rule: Every node is either red or black
Root Rule: The root is always black
Red Rule: Red nodes cannot have red children (no two consecutive red nodes)
Black Rule: Every path from a node to its descendant leaves contains the same number of black nodes
Null Leaves: All null/leaf nodes are considered black
